# Phase 3 OCR Accuracy Repair — 2026-10-26

## Change made

Tightened the localized-XP-versus-row-geometry comparison in `src/reward-geometry.js` and wired that shared rule into `src/bot.js`.

Previously, any XP value with three or more digits was treated as matching a longer geometry anchor when it was a prefix of that anchor. That made a truncated read such as `143` look acceptable against `143907`, so the independent width/PSM crop sweep could be skipped. The same pattern can hide other truncations, such as `405` against `4056`.

The updated rule accepts an exact value match, or the one documented exception: a five-digit XP read that equals the first five digits of a six-digit row token. Shorter prefixes now disagree with the anchor and can trigger the existing bounded crop sweep. The sweep still requires the current multi-width, multi-PSM quorum; the patch does not inject ground-truth answers, trim digits to match annotations, or weaken exact-match acceptance.

## Regression coverage

Added unit coverage for:

- `143` versus `143907`: mismatch, so recovery must not be suppressed.
- `14390` versus `143907`: accepted under the specific five-of-six XP exception.
- `405` versus `4056`: mismatch.
- Exact matching values and other reward-field prefixes.

No expected values or fixture annotations were changed. Existing historical test logs and acceptance reports were preserved.

